      "dom_id": "question-36110",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Identify the surface $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-25{z}^{2}+16x+50z+91=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-25{z}^{2}+16x+50z+91 & =0 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+4x)+{y}^{2}-25({z}^{2}-2z)+91 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x+2)^{2}-4]+{y}^{2}-25[(z-1)^{2}-1]+91 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}-16+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+25+91 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+100 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-2,0,1).$",
