      "name": null,
      "problem": "Identify the surface $y={x}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis and $a=1,\\,c=2.$",
